{"id":"H4505","lemma":"מְנַחֵם","transliteration":"menachem","sayIt":"me-na-CHEM","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Menahem","meaning":"A king of the Kingdom of Israel, living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.15.14;\nson of: Gadi (H1424);\nfather of: Pekahiah (H6494)\n§ Menahem = \"comforter\"\nson of Gadi and king of the northern kingdom of Israel; slew the usurper Shallum to ascend the throne and reigned for ten years; contemporary with prophets Hosea and Amos","glosses":["menahem","then menahem","son","menahem became"],"count":8,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":14,"renderings":{"bsb":"Then Menahem","kjv":"For Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"Menahem","kjv":"Then Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"son","kjv":"began Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"and Menahem","kjv":"and Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"Menahem","kjv":"And Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":21,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Menahem","kjv":"of Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"And Menahem","kjv":"And Menahem"}},{"chapterId":"2ki-15","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"Menahem became","kjv":"of Menahem"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"2 Kings 15:14","note":"Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, came to Samaria, struck Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, killed him, and reigned in his place.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H1424","lemma":"גָּדִי","transliteration":"gadi","gloss":"Gadi"},{"id":"H6494","lemma":"פְּקַחְיָה","transliteration":"peqachyah","gloss":"Pekahiah"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}